From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roshan Gautam <roshangautam07@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:58:26 +0545
Subject: [PATCH 51/74] deps: update undici to 6.29.1

Node.js 18 bundled undici 5.29.0. The undici 5.x line no longer receives
security fixes, and the advisories fixed in the 6.23.0, 6.24.x, 6.27.0,
6.28.x and 6.29.1 releases shipped with Node.js 20.x/22.x security
releases have no 5.x backports. undici 6.x supports Node.js >= 18.17.

This follows the same 5.x -> 6.x move the v20.x LTS line made in
v20.13.0. Only deps/undici and src/undici_version.h change; the globals
Node.js 18 exposes from undici (fetch, FormData, Headers, Request,
Response) are unchanged.

Refs: https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/december-2025-security-releases
Refs: https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/march-2026-security-releases
Refs: https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/june-2026-security-releases
Refs: https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/july-2026-security-releases
Refs: https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/october-2026-security-releases
Refs: 857be5afa3 (deps: update undici to 6.29.1)
